From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:04:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Add iPad 6 (J71b) touchscreen support

The iPad 6 touch controller speaks the same HBPP boot and contact layout
as the iPad 7 (J172), but its runtime firmware uses the older generation-1
data protocol and the board powers it differently:

- power: reset held, analog rail, 10 ms, LDO, 1 ms, clock, 15 ms; no
  display-sync pins;
- boot: zero preamble at 500 kHz, reset released rather than pulsed;
  like J172 it signals firmware-ready twice;
- runtime: packets are payload+5 bytes (at least 16); the data phase
  transmits the read command, tag and phase 1 with a checksum instead of
  filler, using separate transmit and receive buffers with CPHA cleared
  at 500 kHz above 16 bytes; empty-queue, no-data and control replies
  are not frames; long feature reads use the same framed second phase;
- reports 0x73 and 0x9d are not implemented by this firmware, so the
  J172 property reads and mode writes are skipped when it says so;
- the firmware file carries calibration records; the driver fills them
  from the four calibration properties the bootloader copies from the
  ADT (HBPP 0x104 counts payload words minus one), so the file is the
  same for every unit;
- 1 ms chip-select setup/inactive time, level-low runtime interrupt
  draining up to four reports.

Add a J71B variant that shares the iPad protocol paths and branches only
where J71b differs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 349 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 300 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

